# {{namespace}}

This repository uses the plugin layout owned by `template:structure` and enforced by `template:check`
(https://github.com/{{owner}}/template). Authored skills live once under `.agents/<plugin>/skills/<subject>/SKILL.md`,
with kind in metadata and each skill's scripts and assets beside it. Use a family folder for a cohesive subject
(`state/client/` publishes `state-client`); shared words alone do not require grouping. `.agents/sync_generated.py`, `.agents/sync-generated.ps1`,
`.gitattributes`, `.gitignore`, `CLAUDE.md` and `.github/workflows/ci.yml` are vendored from Template's main branch.
Change them in Template, then run `template:update` to refresh the exact vendored content.

`payloads.json` can ship declared package resources from `.agents/hooks`, any declared canonical plugin's
`.agents/<plugin>/references`, `learning` and `assets` folders, or its discovered skill assets (never `SKILL.md`). Map each
file or directory explicitly. Importable implementation follows the selected language's package layout; Python
uses `python:structure` and `python:modules`. Host-specific discovery
extensions live only at the exact `.agents/plugins/adapters/<host>/<plugin>/<skill>.md` source declared in
`host_adapters`; keep shared instruction in the canonical `SKILL.md`. An extended package keeps its Claude skills in
`skills/` and gets `codex-skills/`, selected by its generated Codex manifest.

`.codex/skills/`, `.claude/skills/`, `.agents/INDEX.md`, both marketplace files and `plugins/*` are generated. Run
`pwsh .agents/sync-generated.ps1` after authored changes and require `pwsh .agents/sync-generated.ps1 -Check`
before delivery.

```powershell
pwsh .agents/sync-generated.ps1
pwsh .agents/sync-generated.ps1 -Check
```

For new skills load `skill:new`; for edits, renames, splits or consolidation load `skill:update`.
Both apply `skill:check`, use the current host native skill creator and remove retired public identities in the same cutover.
The project selects Template in `.agents/plugins.json`; after Git initialization, use Agent's
`agent:plugins` to generate both hosts and complete native admission and installation.

Follow `engineering:docs` when adding or changing a skill or standard. Keep a standard's required `Owns …`
opening, then use a concrete fenced example before additional explanatory prose to settle ambiguous terminology. A
starter's explicit unfinished placeholder is not an example, so replace it with real behaviour before committing
because the guidance-example check rejects it.

{{agents_rules}}
